      <groundspeak:logs>
        <groundspeak:log id="1200337545">
          <groundspeak:date>2023-10-10T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="25790230">MaybeSunshine</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP609 Red Deer 55Ave [FOUND]&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I parked on 45 Street for an adventure lab stage, then happened to notice the existence of a nearby cache and also this cap up the hill to the south. A threefer in about 5 minutes, nice! This older cap is a very easy find (stake AND red paint) in nice condition. Thanks!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="683820650">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-02T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="540154">One Bad Ant</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP609 - Red Deer 55Ave - why go around when you can go straight up? It almost looks like someone drove to this one! Grabbed coffee nearby and off we go again. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Road trip! Iron Phoenix and I had a fantastic caching and capping from Calgary to Red Deer. Thanks for the work you do maintaining the caps outforthehunt.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="683667944">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-02T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="3061435">Iron Phoenix</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP609 - Red Deer 55Ave&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Out for another day of capping and caching with OBA, this time in Red Deer!! &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_big.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; It took a bit to figure out where the best, and shortest, way to get to the cap was, but eventually we parked across the street and walked straight up.  There were some shoes, cardboard, and a couple stakes right next to the cap.  Not sure what they were there for, but we thought it was rather funny just how close they were to the cap! Like they were left as a marker! TFTCap!!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="683268352">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-02T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="12442378">mikefromcanmore</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP609  Red Deer 55Ave -  Had a tough choice here.  Walk over to the brew pub or go and look for the cap.  After much willpower walked and found the cap which was being guarded by a pair of old shoes.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="681994077">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-29T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="553001">Bearberrys Cub</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP609 Red Deer 55Ave

N 52° 15.835 W 113° 49.570&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I wasn't really sure I was going to go to Red Deer this morning until I got up, checked the weather and the brass cap page. Even though the forecast was for some rain, the temperatures were supposed to hit the double digits so I decided to go. For the first few brass caps, I parked and walked around to each of them as they were in fairly close proximity from each other. Besides I needed to get out and stretch my legs. Most were quick finds, although the surface of some of the caps was unreadable. Pictures have been sent to OFTH.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
      </groundspeak:logs>
      <groundspeak:travelbugs />
    </groundspeak:cache>
